<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<section class="wrap medium page-pad prose">
  <p class="eyebrow">The fine print</p>
  <h1 class="display">Privacy policy</h1>
  <%- include('_draft') %>
  <h2>What we store</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your account:</strong> username, name, email address and a scrambled (hashed) version of your password. We never see or store your actual password.</li>
    <li><strong>Your profile:</strong> anything you add — status, crafts, city, school, bio, Letterboxd username and website.</li>
    <li><strong>What you post:</strong> films (links to YouTube or Vimeo, not the videos themselves), credits, recommendations, bulletins and set photos.</li>
    <li><strong>Set photos:</strong> we re-encode every photo and remove its hidden metadata, including GPS location and camera details, before storing it.</li>
    <li><strong>Views:</strong> to rank popular films we count unique daily viewers using a one-way code that changes every day. We do not store your IP address.</li>
    <li><strong>Cookies:</strong> only the ones needed to keep you signed in, protect forms, and remember light or dark mode. No advertising or tracking cookies.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <p>We don't sell your data, show ads, or share your email with other members. Bulletin contact details are shown only to signed-in members with a confirmed email.</p>
  <h2>Services we use</h2>
  <p>Hosting (Render), database, photo storage and network protection (Cloudflare), email delivery (Resend) and error reporting (Sentry). Error reports exclude passwords, cookies and form contents. Embedded films are served by YouTube or Vimeo under their own privacy policies; we use their privacy-enhanced players.</p>
  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>From <a href="/settings/account">Account &amp; privacy</a> you can download everything we hold about you, change your email or password, sign out of every device, or permanently delete your account. Deleting removes your profile, films, recommendations, bulletins and photos; credits on other people's films remain as your name only.</p>
  <h2>How long we keep things</h2>
  <p>Your data stays until you delete it or your account. Expired sign-in sessions are removed automatically. Database backups are kept for up to 14 days.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions or requests: <em>[privacy contact email — to be added]</em>.</p>
</section>
<%- include('../partials/foot') %>
